  "question": {
    "text": "A helicopter flying horizontally with a speed of $360 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$ at an altitude of 2 km , drops an object at an instant. The object hits the ground at a point O , 20 s after it is dropped. Displacement of ' O ' from the position of helicopter where the object was released is :<br/>(use acceleration due to gravity $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ and neglect air resistance)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{5} \\mathrm{~km}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "4 km",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "7.2 km",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~km}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0005_79b4cd1e5482.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{u}=360 \\times \\frac{5}{18}=100 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{u} \\times \\mathrm{t}=2 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~m} \\\\ & \\mathrm{t}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{H}}{\\mathrm{g}}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{H}=\\frac{\\mathrm{t}^2 \\mathrm{~g}}{2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{H}=\\frac{400 \\times 10}{2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{H}=2000 \\mathrm{~m} \\\\ & \\mathrm{D}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{H}^2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{D}=2 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~km}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}